>2) Regarding polypiling: just wondering whether anyone actually saw my
>suggestion that polymorph wands convert other wands into traps; there seems
>to have been no reply to this, which seems odd, given that "leave things 
>the way they are" generates 50 rebuttals and responses every time it is 
>posted.  This would neatly solve the wishing/polymorph synergy problem, as
>well as give the player a way of introducing traps.
>
>		-- Ryan S. Borgstrom

I still dont think I like the idea of full blown wand to trap capability, but
if it is going to occur then the polymorph wand->trap is excellent.  I would
make it a chance (I know %%%%%%% always %) of firing and making a trap and
a chance of not firing.  I like having the chance of getting lucky (i.e. wand
of wishing) but would like to see a risk in polypiling.  It seems appropriate
that if you want to polypile 60 wands, you may get your wand of wishing but
may get flamed 30 times :)

